<ansi fg="header">Help for retreat</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">retreat [exit]</ansi>  withdraw your whole company from its fight through [exit].
<ansi fg="command">retreat</ansi>         use the first open exit, in alphabetical order.
<ansi fg="command">flee</ansi>            the same order; <ansi fg="command">flee [exit]</ansi> works too.

Retreat is the only way out of a battle, and your company leaves together.
It also ends a fight with another player. Without companions, you withdraw
alone by the same rules. <ansi fg="command">set wimpy</ansi> orders it for you when your health
runs low.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Two rounds</ansi>
One combat round prepares the withdrawal; the next attempts the escape.
Ordering it again keeps the countdown. Your own attacks stop meanwhile, but
your companions fight on. If the attempt fails, the fight goes on, and you
may order another retreat.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The chance</ansi>
The slowest member present, you included, sets the company's mobility:
Speed, cut by personal burden (up to 60%) and lasting wounds (up to 30%).
Every active foe of your battle pursues, whoever it is striking; the
fastest sets the pursuit, and players fighting you pursue too. Groups
waiting their turn do not pursue.
  chance = 30 + 70 x mobility / (mobility + pursuit), plus cover
It stays between 30% and 95%. With no pursuer, the company gets away.
A failed attempt names the foe who cut you off.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Guardian cover</ansi>
In the preparation round, one guardian with a guard left spends that guard
and its attack to cover the withdrawal: +15 points. A chanting guardian
cannot cover, and cover is lost if that guardian falls or is pinned before
the attempt. Other guards still stop blows as usual (<ansi fg="command">help guardian</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Nobody is left behind</ansi>
A living member who cannot move (hobbled, hamstrung, tackled, or winded)
pins the whole company: the order is refused, or lapses at
the next round, and names who is pinned. These hurts last a few rounds;
order the retreat again when they pass. The same goes for you. Locks,
missing exits and room permissions are checked again every round, and a
member transferred or moved elsewhere cancels the order.

Fallen companions stay where they fell and keep the usual resurrection
rules (<ansi fg="command">help resurrect</ansi>). A companion who lost nerve and fled keeps
their saved return, as <ansi fg="command">help morale</ansi> describes. Companions who join after
the order, other companies, and temporary charms do not come along.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Getting away</ansi>
A successful withdrawal moves the same companions with you, ends your
battle, and clears its targets, chants, and guards. A chant cut short this
way returns no mana. Other players' battles continue. Your horses and
cargo are not in the room, so nothing about them changes. A restart or
copyover cancels an order in progress; it never moves a saved company.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help guardian</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help burden</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help morale</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>.
